    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Description\n\nCurrently, the user can add icons to the completion list using `MiniIcons.tweak_lsp_kind`. \n\nPersonally, I find icons most useful when they are first in the list.\nIt's possible with a little [tweaking](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/088d67751584e4168f35bca89bad70ada7ea4636/lua/mini/completion.lua#L1253):\n\n```lua\nlocal completefunc_lsp = MiniCompletion.completefunc_lsp\nMiniCompletion.completefunc_lsp = function(findstart, base)\n  local res = completefunc_lsp(findstart, base)\n\n  -- Shows the icon first in the completion list:\n  if res and type(res) == \"table\" and #res > 0 and res[1].abbr then\n    for _, item in ipairs(res) do\n      local abbr = MiniIcons.get(\"lsp\", item.kind) .. \" \" .. item.abbr\n      item.abbr = abbr\n    end\n  end\n\n  return res\nend\n```\n\nWould you consider an extra configuration option to achieve this?",
