            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nIt feels like adding this kind of tweaking is a bit too much. Icons are for `kind` property which have a dedicated string property in complete-items, so their place is there. Plus they will be colored, while they won't be if part of `abbr` (with current implementation).\n\nI did think about the idea of providing something like `lsp_completion.process_pmenu_items` which would have solved this kind of issues (both icon and highlighting), but it has too much overlap with `lsp_completion.process_items` and mostly adds confusion for relatively small gain. Maybe if in the future there are new use cases which can't be solved with existing features, it might be added.\n\nThere is a 95% solution with `process_items`:\n\n```lua\n-- NOTE: This relies on `MiniIcons.tweak_lsp_kind` not yet executed.\n-- Otherwise, collect `id -> name` information from the `name -> id` part.\nlocal kinds = vim.deepcopy(vim.lsp.protocol.CompletionItemKind)\n\nlocal process_items = function(items, base)\n  local res = MiniCompletion.default_process_items(items, base)\n  for _, item in ipairs(res) do\n    -- Make sure that icon doesn't appear where it can matter\n    item.insertText = item.insertText or item.label\n    item.filterText = item.filterText or item.label\n    item.sortText = item.sortText or item.label\n    item.label = MiniIcons.get('lsp', kinds[item.kind] or 'Unknown') .. ' ' .. item.label\n  end\n  return res\nend\nrequire('mini.completion').setup({ lsp_completion = { process_items = process_items } })\n```\n\nPossible issue here is that a 'completionItem/resolve' request will used an item with modified label. Which seems to be handled fine for at least some common LSP servers. If that doesn't work, monkey-patching is also a solution here.\n\nClosing as not planned.",
